files[1]{path,scope}:
  src/sdk/query/list.ts,project
body: "## Observed (pm 2026.10.19)\n\n#1481 added the sort key to the brief projection when `--sort <field>` is given. The **default** sort has the same gap, and it is the path agents hit most often (`pm list --status open`, the deprecated `pm list-open`, the AGENTS.md quickstart):\n\n```console\n$ pm list --status open --limit 3\nitems[3]{id,status,type,title}:\n  pm-cli-website-e8fs,open,Decision,pm is context management for any agent …\n  pm-cli-website-xuvj,open,Task,Roll out canonical hoisted merge-driver guard …\n  pm-cli-website-nodo,open,Issue,Fleet release provenance can name the workflow trigger …\nsorting:\n  sort: \"default\"\n  order: \"asc\"\n\n$ pm list --status open --limit 8 --fields id,priority,updated_at\n  pm-cli-website-e8fs,0,\"2026-10-18T06:59:09.673Z\"\n  pm-cli-website-xuvj,0,\"2026-09-26T17:29:15.963Z\"\n  …\n  pm-cli-website-4d5h,1,\"2026-10-19T12:25:28.219Z\"\n```\n\nThe full default comparator groups nonterminal items before terminal items, then sorts by priority ascending, `updated_at` descending, and finally ID ascending (using the existing ID comparator). A status-filtered open list hides the terminal grouping but does not remove it from the unfiltered default contract. Neither key is in the brief rows, and `sorting.sort: \"default\"` does not say what \"default\" means. An agent that reads `.priority` from `--json` gets nothing for every row. In this session an orientation script printed `None` as the priority of all 107 open items and sorted them by an absent key. The agent then needed a second call with `--fields` to recover the ranking the first call had already applied.\n\n## Proposal\n\n- Preserve the compatible legacy `sorting.sort: \"default\"` / `order: \"asc\"` fields and add ordered effective-key metadata covering every comparator stage: terminal-status grouping (`nonterminal_before_terminal`, derived from the active status registry), `priority` ascending, `updated_at` descending, and `id` ascending. An unfiltered list must disclose all four entries in that order; the synthetic terminal-status key must explicitly describe its grouping semantics instead of pretending to be an ordinary stored field. The final field names are a design choice, while completeness and ordering are contract requirements.\n- Under `--brief` (the default list projection), add `priority` as one extra column when the effective sort includes it, exactly as #1481 does for an explicit `--sort`. In TOON that is a single digit per row. Record it in `projection.fields` so the omission receipt stays accurate. `updated_at` can stay behind the receipt, since it is a tiebreak.\n- An explicit `--fields` stays authoritative, as in #1481.\n\nToken cost: about 2 bytes per row. It saves the second `--fields` round trip that every triage pass makes today."
